Error [jet.TypeAsValue]: `Rock` is a type, not a value
  --> tests/ui/type_used_as_value.jet:6:8
    |
  6 |     t: Rock
    |        ^^^^
 Why: A type describes values but is not one; it has no value to bind, pass, return, store or print.
 Fix: Build a value such as `Rock{…}`, or read a compile-time fact of the type, such as `Rock.$fields`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0636

